Z||000008||MinnGreenGT||08-29-2001||01:32 PM||||Hartz- I haven't worked on mine yet, but I've heard that just using a strong smc-adhesive (search forum for panel repair- they show a specific type) to glue it to the lid, then using fiberglass filler to close the gaps.  Sand well and paint!<P>EDIT: Check this thread <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/010081.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/010081.html</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fbr.jpg"> <BR>this is the stuff they recommended.<BR>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 08-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||jch82||08-29-2001||02:34 PM||||I am planning on getting the zr-1 hood scoop from <A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A>  in the near future. I asked Pat about attaching the scoop to my hood and this is what he said...<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>some people use the stuff called "vette adhesive". i use a 2 part agent that looks like epoxy. it is made<BR>for fiberglass and plastic.  i will look for the name.  i think it is made by 3m.  it is tested at 110 mph, several times.  no cracks found yet.  i drive about 75-80 mph on highway.  this is one good stuff.<P>thanks<BR>pat k<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
