Z||000015||qwikgta||08-29-2001||09:01 PM||||Montana,<BR>  You just have to keep checking Ebay,  I just got mine 2 weeks ago.  When I was looking there were 3 for sale.  I got mine (82 Mustang) for $20 and $8 for shipping.  Trust me...I recommend that you get a "genuine" ford part.  I bought a fiberglass one from MPMotorsports and it was ****, (IMO)  I love this one, it has the FORD part number and everything, it just is better quality.  Just go to ebay and type scoop in the search, then look for a mustang one.  Within a week or two there will be one.<P>Rob<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/my_engine_and_stuff0002.jpg"> <BR>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents. <A HREF="http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject" TARGET=_blank>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject</A>     <A HREF="http://www.vafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.vafieros.com</A> <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by qwikgta (edited 08-30-2001).]||||reg||1
